---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CaseStudyHeader from '../../components/CaseStudyHeader.astro';
import EvidencePanel from '../../components/EvidencePanel.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../../components/ContactCTA.astro';

const facts = [
  { num: '3', lbl: 'Distinct private operations' },
  { num: '21', lbl: 'Configured agent roles in the 19 Oct 2026 internal inventory' },
  { num: '217', lbl: 'Recorded issues — not released product features' },
  { num: '122', lbl: 'Recorded AI-CEO decision documents — not human employees or customer deliverables' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Making multi-agent work accountable — Fabio Valente"
  description="Case study: a governed Paperclip + Hermes environment with scoped agent responsibilities, independent review, documented decisions, and approval gates."
>
  <CaseStudyHeader
    num="01"
    title="Making multi-agent work accountable"
    status="AI WORKFLOWS / OPERATIONAL PRIVATE ENVIRONMENT"
    lead="Multiple AI workers can produce a lot of activity without producing accountable work. I designed and operated a private Paperclip and Hermes environment to make responsibilities, handoffs, quality review, and authorization explicit."
  >
    <div class="facts-row">
      {facts.map((f) => (
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="num">{f.num}</div>
          <div class="lbl">{f.lbl}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </CaseStudyHeader>

  <div class="container case-body">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Context and problem</h2>
      <p>
        A multi-agent environment needs safeguards against duplicate missions, unclear ownership,
        recursive task generation, excessive model usage, and self-approved outputs. The challenge
        was not to maximize the agent count; it was to make specialized roles useful, reviewable,
        and bounded.
      </p>

      <h2>What was designed and operated</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Separate workstreams for research and commercial/operational tasks.</li>
        <li>Defined agent roles, mission briefs, task ownership, written handoffs, and execution constraints.</li>
        <li>A task-control layer paired with an AI execution gateway and event-driven routing.</li>
        <li>Separation between worker execution, reviewing, and approval.</li>
        <li>Approval boundaries for spending, external publishing, financial actions, and any other consequential step.</li>
        <li>Documented issues, decision records, QA checks, exceptions, and human intervention paths.</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="diagram-panel">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 640 470" role="img" aria-label="Governance diagram: incoming request flows through scoped mission, task coordination in Paperclip, execution via the Hermes gateway, specialist AI workers, independent QA review, human approval for consequential actions, and a documented outcome. A side route lets QA send work back for revision or rejection.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="arr1" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto">
              <path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#3E5C76"></path>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <style>
            .n { fill:#FFFFFF; stroke:#C9CFD6; }
            .g { fill:#EDF1F5; stroke:#3E5C76; }
            .w { fill:#F7F1E6; stroke:#8A6D3B; }
            .t { fill:#23282E; font:600 13px Manrope,sans-serif; }
            .s { fill:#7A7F86; font:500 10px 'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.08em; }
            .a { stroke:#3E5C76; stroke-width:1.6; fill:none; }
          </style>
          <rect class="n" x="220" y="10" width="200" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="320" y="30" text-anchor="middle">Incoming request / trigger</text>
          <text class="s" x="320" y="45" text-anchor="middle">EVENT-DRIVEN</text>
          <path class="a" d="M320,54 L320,72" marker-end="url(#arr1)"></path>

          <rect class="n" x="220" y="74" width="200" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="320" y="94" text-anchor="middle">Scoped mission</text>
          <text class="s" x="320" y="109" text-anchor="middle">ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA</text>
          <path class="a" d="M320,118 L320,136" marker-end="url(#arr1)"></path>

          <rect class="n" x="220" y="138" width="200" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="320" y="158" text-anchor="middle">Task coordination</text>
          <text class="s" x="320" y="173" text-anchor="middle">PAPERCLIP</text>
          <path class="a" d="M320,182 L320,200" marker-end="url(#arr1)"></path>

          <rect class="n" x="220" y="202" width="200" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="320" y="222" text-anchor="middle">Agent gateway</text>
          <text class="s" x="320" y="237" text-anchor="middle">HERMES</text>
          <path class="a" d="M320,246 L320,264" marker-end="url(#arr1)"></path>

          <rect class="n" x="220" y="266" width="200" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="320" y="286" text-anchor="middle">Specialist AI workers</text>
          <text class="s" x="320" y="301" text-anchor="middle">SCOPED ROLES</text>
          <path class="a" d="M320,310 L320,328" marker-end="url(#arr1)"></path>

          <rect class="n" x="220" y="330" width="200" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="320" y="350" text-anchor="middle">Independent reviewer / QA</text>
          <text class="s" x="320" y="365" text-anchor="middle">SEPARATE FROM WORKERS</text>
          <path class="a" d="M320,374 L320,392" marker-end="url(#arr1)"></path>

          <rect class="w" x="220" y="394" width="200" height="40" rx="20"></rect>
          <text class="t" x="320" y="418" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8A6D3B">Human approval [consequential]</text>
          <path class="a" d="M320,434 L320,450" marker-end="url(#arr1)" display="none"></path>

          <text class="t" x="320" y="462" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">Documented outcome + audit record</text>

          <path class="a" d="M420,352 C500,352 500,160 424,160" stroke-dasharray="4 4" marker-end="url(#arr1)"></path>
          <text class="s" x="505" y="260" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(90 505 260)">REVISE / REJECT → TASK COORDINATION</text>
        </svg>
        <p class="caption">CONCEPTUAL, SANITIZED WORKFLOW</p>
      </div>

      <h2>My role</h2>
      <p>
        I defined the operating model, agent instructions, mission requirements, authorization
        gates, escalation paths, and acceptance criteria. I reviewed outputs, troubleshot workflow
        issues, coordinated changes, and approved consequential decisions. AI agents produced
        implementation code and some infrastructure fixes; I am not claiming to have independently
        authored all of that code.
      </p>

      <h2>Observed result</h2>
      <p>
        The 19 October 2026 internal audit showed 21 configured roles across three operations,
        alongside task/issue records and decision documents. It demonstrates a structured private
        operating model and an audit trail—not enterprise-level uptime, scale, or a claim that
        every agent role continuously executed production work.
      </p>

      <h2>What I would improve</h2>
      <p>
        Simplify role boundaries further where jobs overlap, formalize failure telemetry, track the
        useful-output-to-cost ratio, and reduce operational complexity without sacrificing review
        or safety.
      </p>

      <div class="limits">
        <h3>Important boundaries / status</h3>
        <p>
          Private, single-machine, founder-operated environment under direct supervision. Not
          independently audited enterprise infrastructure; not a high-availability service; no
          autonomous authority to spend, contact outsiders, or execute real-capital trades.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Evidence</h2>
      <figure class="diagram-panel" style="background:#F5F4F1;">
        <a href="/assets/evidence/workflow-architecture.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Open full-size diagram (2250×1200) in a new tab">
          <img
            src="/assets/evidence/workflow-architecture.png"
            alt="Sanitized conceptual AI-assisted workflow architecture: human owner defines requirements, Paperclip tracks issues and approval gates, Hermes routes AI execution, agent teams research/build/QA, artifacts are produced, human approval authorizes deploy. Cross-cutting controls include private access, structured records, and documented limitations."
            width="2250"
            height="1200"
            loading="eager"
            style="border-radius:8px;"
          />
        </a>
        <p class="caption" style="color:#5a6470;">
          SANITIZED CONCEPTUAL VIEW — PORTFOLIO ABSTRACTION, NOT A FULL NETWORK TOPOLOGY ·
          <a href="/assets/evidence/workflow-architecture.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View full size ↗</a>
        </p>
      </figure>
      <p class="scroll-hint">
        ← Scroll the diagram sideways, or open full size for readable text →
      </p>
      <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-muted);">
        This architecture summary was prepared for portfolio use and explicitly labeled as a
        sanitized abstraction. Source screenshots of the live private environment are not
        published; verified internal artifacts are available upon request.
      </p>
    </div>

    <nav class="case-nav" aria-label="Case study navigation">
      <a href="/work/research-automation/">Next: Turning recurring research into a verifiable workflow →</a>
      <a href="/#work">← Back to selected work</a>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <ContactCTA />
</BaseLayout>
